<title>USA: Penn Traffic chief executive to retire.</title>
<headline>Penn Traffic chief executive to retire.</headline>
<dateline>SYRACUSE, N.Y. 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Penn Traffic Co said Friday that John Dixon would retire as president and chief executive officer on September 30 for personal and health reasons.</p>
<p>The company said it is engaging an executive recruiting firm in a national search to identify and evaluate the best candidate to succeed Dixon.</p>
<p>It said Chairman Gary Hirsch will assume Dixon's responsibilities during the search process.</p>
<p>The presidents of Penn Traffic divisions will report directly to Hirsch during the search, it said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
